From: nuubOS Project <nuubos@localhost>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] control: home button, host MAC and more stream statistics

BUTTONS <hex> on the control channel holds (or with 0 releases) gamepad
buttons on player 1 on top of what its gamepad holds, so the supervising
process can send the Home button the console keeps for its own menu.

The status action reports the MAC address the host advertises (for
Wake-on-LAN), and @stats adds the bytes received, the host processing
latency and the frames lost on the network.
---
diff --color -ruN a/libgamestream/client.c b/libgamestream/client.c
--- a/libgamestream/client.c	2026-10-13 11:56:21.295635352 +0200
+++ b/libgamestream/client.c	2026-10-13 11:56:45.253324293 +0200
@@ -232,6 +232,11 @@
   if (xml_search(data->memory, data->size, "hostname", &server->hostname) != GS_OK)
     server->hostname = NULL;
 
+  // Optional: the MAC address (real only over HTTPS, once paired)
+  server->mac = NULL;
+  if (xml_search(data->memory, data->size, "mac", &server->mac) != GS_OK)
+    server->mac = NULL;
+
   // These fields are present on all version of GFE that this client supports
   if (!strlen(currentGameText) || !strlen(pairedText) || !strlen(server->serverInfo.serverInfoAppVersion) || !strlen(stateText))
     goto cleanup;
